    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance visible from both directions on the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with posts or reflective delineators to make it clearly visible at night or in low visibility conditions.\n• Clear overhanging branches along the driveway to maintain a full-height clearance for fire and rescue apparatus.\n• Trim dense vegetation along the driveway edges to keep sight lines open for approaching responders.\n• Create a designated turnaround area near the residence large enough for a fire engine or ambulance to reverse direction without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Mark the turnaround area clearly so responders can identify it on arrival.\n• Keep the detached structure clearly labeled or numbered if it could be confused with the main residence during an emergency response.\n• Post the property address at a second location near the main residence, visible from the driveway approach.\n• Keep the access drive surface clear of vehicles, equipment, or debris that would block a single-lane approach.\n• Trim vegetation around the detached structure to keep all sides accessible to responders on foot.\n• Keep any perimeter gates along the driveway unlocked or equipped with a Knox Box or responder-accessible lock.\n• Identify and mark a secondary foot-access route across the open terrain in case the driveway becomes blocked."
  },
