    "recommendations": "• Trim tree branches that hang directly over or touch the house and any other structures on the property.\n• Thin trees in clusters close to the house so there is open space between individual trees and between trees and the structure.\n• Remove shrubs growing directly against or within a few feet of the house walls.\n• Clear brush from both sides of the driveway along its full length to keep the travel lane open and visible.\n• Trim overhanging branches above the driveway so vehicles, including fire trucks, can pass through without obstruction.\n• Mow or cut grass growing close to the house down to a short, low height.\n• Separate shrubs from nearby trees by removing or trimming vegetation that connects ground-level plants to tree canopies.\n• Thin mixed vegetation surrounding the house to create open gaps and reduce the amount of plant material immediately around the structure.\n• Clear brush and shrubs from the area around any outbuildings or detached structures on the property.\n• Keep the area at the driveway entrance clear and easy to identify from the main road since there is only one way in and out.\n• Remove dead or dry grass and plant material from around the base of trees near the house.\n• Maintain a clear turning or pull-out area near the house so emergency vehicles can maneuver without backing the full length of the driveway."
  },
